<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Halilaga	   unloading   maize grits     2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Matheus	    unloading   gluten feed	 600     U.S.</p>
<p>Flag Nicolas     arrived     corn	     23,524     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	    8,400</p>
<p>				     soya meal	 3,000</p>
<p>Cemil Taman	21/7	  sunflower meal  2,211     Europe</p>
<p>Amur 2508	  21/7	  barley	    2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Amur 2529	  23/7	  sunflower meal  1,473     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobalt 246    24/7	  barley	    3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Pricor	     27/7	  wheat	    35,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Volgobalt 247    28/7	  barley	    2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Don 2		28/7	  wheat		 991     Europe</p>
<p>Zathay	     30/7	  barley	    2,700     Europe</p>
